  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_cabinpower",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 5910,
        "y": 0
      },
      "text": "CABIN POWER HARNESS - non-ECU: the glove-box fuse box (Option B, _research FUSEBOX-B-SLOT-MAP 2026-10-11): Bussmann LMI, two stacks (lmi_a_*, lmi_b_*, DECISIONS S14), Eaton RFRM 15401-1-2-1-0A (rfrm) and 3x MTA 0301491 (mta1-mta3); the battery feed ring (PDB bus) and the fuel pump run to the trunk. The box lives only in this file. The ECU-switched relays are seated in the box and drawn here (k_fan / k_efi / k_fp on MTA-1, k_str / k_etb on MTA-2, k_fan2 on MTA-3, k_acc in the RFRM, k_eps HCR150 beside the box); their wires land on the module's own relay-position terminals. Fuse -> relay 30 and relay coil+ links are short jumpers inside the box (the MTA 0301491 internal bus is unconfirmed, OPEN-ITEMS row 48). The ECU coil (85) wires stay on ST185-A-cabin / ST185-B-cabin (their ECU pin sets the loom) and arrive broken off. Every feed between this file and A-cabin, B-cabin, CSB3 or EngineRoom-C is drawn broken off in both with a note naming the other file. RFRM / MTA slot numbers are not assigned: cavities are named by circuit."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 5910,
        "y": 600
      },
      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nRFRM EFI86: 5A - relay coil feed, PERMANENT (EFI main relay 86)\nMTA-2 MRS: 7.5A - MRS EPS pump logic enable (fed from k_eps_en 87 per the slot map; k_eps_en not yet in the SoT, OPEN-ITEMS row 40)\nLMI L7: 60A AMI - EPS pump relay 30 (k_eps HCR150, beside the box), Bussmann AMI-60 (60 A, sized 2026-09-28 - sot/channels.csv k_eps c1)\nEFI Main Relay 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Aux 6 / A28 - low-side (Aux 5-8 capable of either; low-side chosen for ECU Hold Power)\nEFI Main Relay 86: Coil + - PERMANENT battery via RFRM EFI86 5A (must stay live after key-off for Hold Power)\nETB Power Relay 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Aux 2 / A20 - LOW-SIDE ONLY (Aux 1-4)\nETB Power Relay 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nFuel Pump Relay 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Aux 3 / A19 - LOW-SIDE ONLY (Aux 1-4)\nFuel Pump Relay 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nRadiator Fan Relay (on/off) 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nStart Relay 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nCondenser Fan Relay (on/off) 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Ign 5 / B13 - low-side, no external flywheel diode or suppression (on/off relay; INFERENCE from the G4X help Auxiliary Output Wiring PWM-only diode advice, not a Link statement) - TE 1-1393304-0, plain relay, no diode (slot map row 9)\nCondenser Fan Relay (on/off) 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nMR-S EHPS pump relay (HCR150,  85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - <- ECU-B B12 (Ign 6) - EPS relay trigger; moved into the cabin 2026-09-28 (Daniel: every relay in the cabin)\nMR-S EHPS pump relay (HCR150,  30: LMI L7 - Bussmann AMI-60 (60 A, sized 2026-09-28 - sot/channels.csv k_eps c1)"
    }
  ],
